01:37:52.140 --> 01:37:55.920
But I think for most people
who are going to sleep at night

01:37:55.920 --> 01:37:58.500
and are trying their best
to sleep well at night

01:37:58.500 --> 01:37:59.550
and are trying their best

01:37:59.550 --> 01:38:01.560
to wake up in the morning at whatever hour

01:38:01.560 --> 01:38:03.300
and stay alert and focused
throughout the day,

01:38:03.300 --> 01:38:04.830
maybe with a brief nap,

01:38:04.830 --> 01:38:06.090
the tools that I talked about today

01:38:06.090 --> 01:38:09.060
related to light,
temperature, food, exercise,

01:38:09.060 --> 01:38:12.390
caffeine, supplements, and digital tools,

01:38:12.390 --> 01:38:15.420
I'm hoping will prove to
be very useful for you.

01:38:15.420 --> 01:38:17.250
They certainly are all supported

01:38:17.250 --> 01:38:19.500
by excellent peer-reviewed research.

01:38:19.500 --> 01:38:21.060
And I should just emphasize again

01:38:21.060 --> 01:38:22.590
that most of the tools we talked about

01:38:22.590 --> 01:38:24.510
