01:38:29.070 --> 01:38:30.390
I really want to encourage everybody

01:38:30.390 --> 01:38:32.250
to get your behaviors right.

01:38:32.250 --> 01:38:35.280
Get all of the things related
to your timing of exercise

01:38:35.280 --> 01:38:36.806
and type of exercise

01:38:36.806 --> 01:38:40.170
in the best possible
order and time of day.

01:38:40.170 --> 01:38:42.450
We talked about this critical
period early in the day

01:38:42.450 --> 01:38:44.460
and then another critical
period in the middle of the day

01:38:44.460 --> 01:38:45.390
and the late afternoon

01:38:45.390 --> 01:38:46.590
and then this third critical period

01:38:46.590 --> 01:38:47.550
in the middle of the night.

01:38:47.550 --> 01:38:50.395
Different tools for the
different three critical periods.

01:38:50.395 --> 01:38:52.905
I promise that if you
start to implement some,

01:38:52.905 --> 01:38:55.470
or ideally, all of these tools,

01:38:55.470 --> 01:38:58.380
the quality of your sleep
will increase tremendously.

01:38:58.380 --> 01:39:00.360
And of course, in doing so,

01:39:00.360 --> 01:39:02.130
the quality of your daytime alertness

01:39:02.130 --> 01:39:04.560
and your ability to focus
will improve tremendously.

01:39:04.560 --> 01:39:08.490
Again, sleep is the absolute foundation

01:39:08.490 --> 01:39:10.320
of your mental health,
your physical health,

01:39:10.320 --> 01:39:12.270
and your performance in all endeavors.

01:39:12.270 --> 01:39:14.940
So if there's one area of your life

01:39:14.940 --> 01:39:17.700
to really focus on and try and optimize,

01:39:17.700 --> 01:39:20.100
